        <UserObject label="" mermaidData="{&#xa;  &quot;data&quot;: &quot;sequenceDiagram\n    actor Sales as \&quot;Sales\&quot;\n    participant UI as \&quot;Interface: UI\&quot;\n    participant Snap as \&quot;mobileSnapshotService: Service\&quot;\n    participant API as \&quot;mainController: Controller\&quot;\n    participant Order as \&quot;orderService: Service\&quot;\n    participant DB as \&quot;PostgreSQL: Database\&quot;\n    Sales-&gt;&gt;UI: Request/refresh offline snapshot\n    UI-&gt;&gt;+API: GET /api/v1/mobile/snapshot with ETag\n    API-&gt;&gt;Snap: Build scoped full snapshot\n    Snap-&gt;&gt;+DB: Read retailer, MLOR, products, prices, campaigns, indicative stock\n    DB--&gt;&gt;-Snap: Versioned data\n    Snap--&gt;&gt;UI: 200 snapshot or 304 Not Modified\n    Sales-&gt;&gt;UI: Press Send for local draft\n    UI-&gt;&gt;+API: POST /api/v1/orders/sync with clientOrderKey\n    API-&gt;&gt;Order: Sync and idempotency check\n    Order-&gt;&gt;+DB: Revalidate scope, base price, campaign and MLOR version\n    alt Conditions unchanged\n        Order-&gt;&gt;+DB: Create order once as PendingApproval\n        API--&gt;&gt;-UI: Synchronized order\n    else Condition conflict\n        API--&gt;&gt;-UI: 409 current conditions; no order created\n    else Same clientOrderKey retry\n        DB--&gt;&gt;-Order: Return existing result\n        API--&gt;&gt;UI: Same order/result\n    end\n    Note over UI,API: No background sync, allocation, reservation or stock rejection during sync.\n\n&quot;,&#xa;  &quot;config&quot;: null,&#xa;  &quot;version&quot;: &quot;12&quot;&#xa;}" id="RnOlWsIO6VAryWkDG1wP-1">
